WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.410
Run one small change with Claude code in SpecWithCode. This

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:08.010
walkthrough prepares the task. It does not submit a provider

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:08.330
run.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:13.050
In Settings, Providers, confirm Claude code on the machine

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.730
that runs the project. Use your existing Claude code login.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.050
If it is not ready, complete its own sign -in before

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:20.470
starting.

00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:24.757
Open an example repository as a project. The main

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:28.817
conversation is the project coordinator. Check which machine

00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:29.737
is doing the work.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:34.310
Select Claude Code, an available model, and the approval mode

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:38.050
you intend to use. This tutorial does not require full

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:38.450
access.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.750
Give it one bounded task. Add a named greeting, keep the no

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.150
argument greeting working, and add tests for both. Ask it to

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.970
describe the change before editing.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:55.177
Read the proposed change, then ask it to implement. Review

00:00:55.177 --> 00:00:58.177
any command approval rather than accepting it automatically.

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:03.497
Inspect the changed files and the actual test output. If a

00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:07.517
check failed or was not run, keep that in the result. A

00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:09.997
confident reply is not test evidence.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.890
Finish with the change, its diff, and actual test evidence.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.930
Use SpecWeave increments when you need a durable plan and

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.030
task record. They are optional for this first task.
